      "attribution": "Adunni Olorisha Trust / Adunni Osun Foundation",
      "observation": "The published tour camera sees the back of the iron leaves, the pedestrian arch and the sheltered passage, giving a shared coordinate and bearings for both parts. The view beneath the entrance gable shows tightly spaced reed courses changing direction across the framed triangular panels."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://artsandculture.google.com/asset/arugb%C3%A1-gate/-AG5YC4vDTPDRg",
      "attribution": "CyArk / Adunni Olorisha Trust / Adunni Osun Foundation",
      "observation": "The gate opens onto the narrow path toward Ojúbọ Òṣogbo and was restored in 2017–18. The photographed front has raised lips around the side recesses, an uneven lower jamb, a dark ribbed throat and patchy damp staining around the footing."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://whc.unesco.org/uploads/nominations/1118.pdf",
      "attribution": "National Commission for Museums and Monuments, Nigeria",
      "observation": "The ritual footpath runs separately from the main pilgrimage road. The broad road geometry in the retained tiles supplies no distinct gate or parallel footpath on which to set a bearing."
    },
    {
      "url": "https://artsandculture.google.com/asset/arugb%C3%A1-gate-susanne-wenger-and-adebisi-akanji/ewEG54QkAFFOhA",
      "attribution": "CyArk / Adunni Olorisha Trust / Adunni Osun Foundation",
      "date": "2019",
      "observation": "The oblique roadside view shows a low saddle between elevated front and rear gable tips, dark ribbing above and timber spars below. A separate sculpted arch and closed metal gate stand along the road in front of the shelter.",
      "imageHash": "sha256:903a98132ec7890a6f80985e222caf920e4d443aff30c6745defc1f0b0ea6bcd"
    },
    {
      "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Osun_Sacred_Grove_forest_Osogbo_Main_Gate.jpg",
      "attribution": "Wikimedia Commons photograph of the inner gate frontage",
